 my community I knew  that leaving the EU would be worse off  for my community for jobs for local  businesses but I do wholeheartedly  accept that we are leaving the EU and  now the job moving forward is to stare  the Conservative Party in the eye to  look at Boris Johnson and stand up for  our workers rights our environmental  protections our security our food  standards  and as deputy leader that's the fight  that I will take that I will say this  Sophie I grew up in poverty I know what  hunger feels like I know it being cold  feels like and my lived experiences will  enable me to connect with voters around  the country  it hasn't matter that I'm from London so  it's not just you say it's more about in  the experience that you've had rather  than the location that you grow up -  absolutely and I work on our front line  NHS I'm fighting our government and cuts  every single day when I work as an A&amp;E  doctor the Labour Party changed my life  it enabled a mixed-race woman from a  single-parent background whose mum had  to work three jobs to put food on the  table  - then despite failing her a-levels and  feeling like she was lost of all hope to  go on and go to Cambridge to study  medicine age 24 because a Labour Party  believed in her I want to stand for  deputy leader because I want to I want  to show every child in this country that  there's no ceiling on what they can  achieve there was a ceiling placed on me  and my family under Thatcher and major  governments and I'm determined to smash  that ceiling for all the children who's  you know for whom the door closed on the  12th labour failing those children now  Labour's not failing the Conservative  government have been failing in a loser  for the last election ten years Corbin's  we need a Labour government and you're  right  people didn't trust us to govern and as  deputy leader I'm going to go into the  communities up and down the country into  Scotland into Wales roll up my sleeves  Alec Ison and that's the pitch I just  want to bring it back to reality  slightly with the latest polling this is  the latest polling on the deputy  leadership poll from you gov you're  there an 80% yes way out in front  well 57% is Angela Rayner I mean on this  score she would win in the first round  what I mean is it effectively game over  for me well for all of you you've part  from Angela Raina it's never game over  it's never game over Sophie I've I've  been the underdog my whole life I've  always been told that there things I  can't achieve because of who I am and  where I come from I've never listened  before I'm never gonna listen now but  you know what the fact that I'm on the  show with you this morning if there is  one child that turns on the TV and says  oh my goodness she was poor she was  hungry she was cold she failed  she felt a void of hope but she's able  to go on and achieve and go from poverty  to Parliament if there's one child  that's influenced by my story it doesn't  matter that I'm on 8% because I'm  winning being right here getting those  messages out okay and I'm keen to get  your thoughts on the leadership contest  who do you want to win I genuinely will  work with whoever the leader is and I'm  actually the only deputy leader that  didn't nominate a leadership candidate  who do you want to win I don't have an  opinion at this point because I think  over the entire cabinet job with one of  the winners then listen would I love to  be in a she had a secretary state for  health given my NHS background given the  fact I'm fighting in A&amp;E all the time  doing shifts of course I'd love that but  more importantly to hear women I think  it makes me the right person for the job  I would really like to see a woman at  the top of the party now but  fundamentally we have a rebuilding  process that is going to take years it's  going to require listening it's going to  require working together and it's got to  be about the best person for the job but  it's going to be exciting the next few  weeks seeing you know people setting out  their stall is it's yeah yes it's gonna  be interesting  okay I'm keen to are shoe quickly and  about a story that was in The Sunday  Times today it's about reports that  Jeremy Corbyn is planning to nominate  his chief of staff Kerry Murphy for a  peerage do you think it's appropriate  that someone so closely involved with  the last election campaign should be  elevated to the House of Lords I  personally don't know Kerry Murphy well  at all what I do know is that she's  currently being investigated by the eh  RC and I made clear yesterday that as  deputy leader I would take onboard every  single recommendation from the ear  eh r c-- news on allegations of  anti-semitism and how they were done yes  and hope not hey said that anyone who is  being investigated by the eh RC  shouldn't be recommended for a peerage  so I think that does need to be taken  seriously so you're a bit uncomfortable  with it I would like to see the outcome  of the EHR scene report and I don't know  Kerry Murphy personally okay now just to  finish I thought because you know not  all of our viewers will have a clear  impression of who you are we could end  with a little quick fire round okay okay  oh are you ready I'm ready are you ready  okay William and Kate or Harry and Megan  Harry and Megan  Love Actually or love Island Oh both I  like both yeah because I did the Love  Actually video but I do I do like love  Islands okay and boxing or football  boxing favorite member of the  Conservative Party  Tracy Crouch and political hero oh come  at Lee

